{title: Chief Iram}
{subtitle: Genesis 36:43; 1 Chronicles 1:54; Genesis 36:1–9; 36:40–43}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm] [F6] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]This is the family history of E[Gm]sau
That is [Eb]Edom in the hill country of [Bb]Seir
He took his wives from the daughters of Ca[Gm]naan
A[Eb]dah and Oholi[F]bamah and Ba[Bb]semath came
[Eb]Their possessions were [F]too great to live to[Bb]gether
[Eb]The land could not sup[F]port their live[Gm]stock
So Esau [Eb]settled in the hill [F]country of [Gm]Seir
Esau is [Eb]Edom the [F]father of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Chief Iram [Eb]stands in the list of the [Bb]chiefs
These were the [Eb]chiefs of Edom
Ac[Gm]cording to their settle[F]ments in the land they [Eb]possessed
This was [Bb]Esau the [F]father of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
By their clans and their regions name by [Gm]name
Chief [Eb]Timna and Chief Alvah are [Bb]known
Chief Oholibamah and Chief Elah [Gm]too
Chief [Eb]Pinon and Chief [F]Kenaz ap[Bb]pear
[Eb]These are the chiefs [F]descended from E[Bb]sau
In the [Eb]land they pos[F]sessed and [Gm]held
The [Eb]genealogy con[F]firms his po[Gm]sition there
A[Eb]mong the tribal [F]chiefs of the [Bb]land
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In the book of Chronicles the name is re[Gm]peated
Chief [Eb]Magdiel and Chief Iram are list[Bb]ed
Confirming his place [F/A]in the tribal struc[Gm]ture
The [Eb]spread of Esau’s de[F]scendants is [Bb]seen
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Chief I[Eb]ram in the [Gm]land of Edom
This was [Bb]Esau the [F]father of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_verse}
